// PIN (2026-06-13): auto-disposal SHOULD insert `free(s)` at scope exit, so a
// locally-owned String never needs a manual discharge. It doesn't — a `<view!>`
// String has TWO matching discharge options (`free` matches `view|instance`,
// `take` matches `view`), neither marked `[!]`, so `selectDisposal` can't pick a
// winner and the auto-discharger errors KORU030 "multiple discharge options...
// Discharge explicitly" (auto_discharge_inserter.zig:707) instead of inserting
// the free.
//
// This is 610_008_parse_int VERBATIM minus the trailing `|> std/string:free(s)`.
// 610_008 is green WITH the explicit free; this must go green WITHOUT it once
// the auto-disposer can choose `free`. Fix candidate: mark `std/string:free` as
// the `[!]` default disposer so `selectDisposal` prefers it over `take`.
~import std/string
~import std/io

~std/string:from-page(text: "42")
| ok s |> std/string:parse-int(s)
    | ok n  |> std/io:print.ln("{{ n:d }}")
    | err e |> std/io:print.ln("{{ e:s }}")
| err _ |> _
